---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import WebGLBackground from "../components/WebGLBackground.jsx";
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, "");
---

<Layout title="About Us — RBSMUN 2026">
    <WebGLBackground client:only="react" />

    <nav class="glass-nav" id="mainNav">
        <div class="nav-inner">
            <a href={`${base}/`} class="nav-logo"
                ><img src={`${base}/images/logo.webp`} alt="RBSMUN Logo" /></a
            >
            <div class="nav-links" id="navLinks">
                <a href={`${base}/`}>Home</a>
                <a href={`${base}/about`} class="active">About Us</a>
                <a href={`${base}/committees`}>Committees</a>
                <a href={`${base}/conference`}>Conference Details</a>
                <a href={`${base}/team`}>Our Team</a>
            </div>
            <a
                href="https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLScHRl-Q3-XBSMNHwiufUyGBYGU-MBBVO2-GGSOJL0atyxPcKg/viewform"
                target="_blank"
                class="nav-cta">Register →</a
            >
            <button class="nav-toggle" id="navToggle" aria-label="Toggle menu">
                <span></span><span></span><span></span>
            </button>
        </div>
    </nav>

    <section
        class="page-hero"
        style={`background-image: url('${base}/images/miscellaneous/About+us+pg+background.webp');`}
    >
        <div class="hero-bg-overlay"></div>
        <div class="container">
            <h1 class="page-hero-title">About RBSMUN</h1>
            <p class="page-hero-subtitle">
                Discover the history and values behind one of the most
                prestigious Model United Nations conferences in Nepal.
            </p>
        </div>
    </section>

    <div class="content-wrapper">
        <section class="section">
            <div class="container" style="max-width: 1100px;">
                <div class="section-header" data-anim="reveal">
                    <h2 class="section-title">
                        What is <span class="text-gradient">RBSMUN</span>?
                    </h2>
                </div>
                <div
                    class="glass-card"
                    style="padding: 3rem;"
                    data-anim="fade-up"
                >
                    <div class="card-glow"></div>
                    <p
                        style="color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.9; margin-bottom: 1.5rem; font-size: 1.05rem;"
                    >Since its genesis in 2005, Rato Bangala School Model United Nations (RBSMUN)has been a consistent platform for enthusiastic students from Nepal and beyond to strategize, discover, and grow. Our principal, Miss Milan Dixit, organized the first-ever RBSMUN with the belief that bringing Model UN to Rato Bangala School and Nepal would enable students to grow,  intellectually, socially, and cognitively. Since then, RBS has held its MUN  annually and become one of the most prestigious MUN conferences in the country. It has evolved from an in-school activity to an interschool conference, and, more recently, with its promise of high calibre deliberation and negotiation to an international conference.
                    </p>
                    <p
                        style="color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.9; font-size: 1.05rem; margin-bottom: 1.5rem;"
                    >During Model UN conferences, students transcend the four walls of classrooms and the finite pages of books. Serving as the diplomats of  countries from all over the world, students tackle complex real-world issues ranging from regional conflicts to environmental problems, and, in the process, develop an invaluable understanding of events that shape our world.
                    </p>

                    <p
                        style="color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.9; font-size: 1.05rem; margin-bottom: 1.5rem;"
                    >Over the years, RBSMUN has created generations of thoughtful citizens who care about people’s sufferings and care enough to take steps towards a shared future of peace. This year, we hope to continue fostering our precedent: inspiring change. Providing a place for ardent delegates to develop their passions and to share their ideas, we strive to change the status quo. Believing that having a good future requires grooming knowledgeable and dutiful global citizens, RBSMUN provides an opportunity to learn about historic, current, and futuristic world events; to understand their causes, dimensions, and implications; to build a well-informed opinion about the current state of  political, economic, natural, and social affairs; to articulate those stances; to persuade; and to galvanise change for all.  
                    </p>

                    <p
                        style="color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.9; font-size: 1.05rem;"
                    >Each year, we host a new group of debaters who, at the end of the conference, emerge intrigued, impassioned, and ready to take the reins of  the world in their hands. In this iteration of RBSMUN, we will continue our tradition of excellence, inspiration to growth, and enlightenment of perspective. Join us this December to witness the world of RBS Model UN come to life, and to change your life with its stimulus.  
                    </p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section class="section section-textured">
            <div class="container" style="max-width: 1100px;">
                <div
                    class="section-header"
                    style="text-align: center;"
                    data-anim="reveal"
                >
                    <h2 class="section-title">
                        Message from the <span class="text-gradient"
                            >Principal</span
                        >
                    </h2>
                </div>
                <div
                    class="glass-card"
                    style="padding: clamp(1.5rem, 5vw, 3rem);"
                    data-anim="fade-up"
                >
                    <div class="card-glow"></div>
                    <div class="principal-layout">
                        <div class="principal-image-col">
                            <div class="principal-image-wrapper">
                                <img
                                    src={`${base}/images/miscellaneous/principal.webp`}
                                    alt="Principal"
                                />
                            </div>
                            <p
                                style="color: var(--text-secondary); font-family: var(--font-heading); font-size: 0.9rem; margin-top: 0.75rem; text-align: center; letter-spacing: 0.02em;"
                            >
                                Milan Dixit
                            </p>
                            <p
                                style="color: var(--text-ghost); font-family: var(--font-heading); font-size: 0.7rem; text-align: center; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.1em;"
                            >
                                Principal, Rato Bangala School
                            </p>
                        </div>
                        <div class="principal-text-col">
                            <p
                                style="color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.9; font-size: 1.05rem; font-style: italic;"
                            >
                                "It is my pleasure to welcome you to the
                                twenty-first edition of the Rato Bangala School
                                Model United Nations. This student-led
                                conference provides an exceptional platform for
                                thoughtful dialogue, diplomacy, and engagement
                                with both local and global issues.
                            </p>
                            <p
                                style="color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.9; font-size: 1.05rem; font-style: italic; margin-top: 1.5rem;"
                            >
                                At its core, Model United Nations promotes the
                                ideals of peace, justice, human rights, and
                                responsible leadership. Through research,
                                negotiation, and debate, delegates strengthen
                                their critical thinking, communication,
                                collaboration, and problem-solving skills while
                                gaining a deeper understanding of the challenges
                                facing our interconnected world.
                            </p>
                            <p
                                style="color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.9; font-size: 1.05rem; font-style: italic; margin-top: 1.5rem;"
                            >
                                This year's theme selected by the organising
                                students,<strong>
                                    Unity and Inclusion in a Fragmented World</strong
                                >, is both timely and relevant. It encourages
                                delegates to explore how cooperation, empathy,
                                and inclusive leadership can help address the
                                divisions and complexities of our time.
                            </p>
                            <p
                                style="color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.9; font-size: 1.05rem; font-style: italic; margin-top: 1.5rem;"
                            >
                                The fifteen committees reflect this spirit
                                through a diverse range of stimulating topics,
                                from cyber warfare and state accountability to
                                sovereign debt and the future of global finance.
                                The International Press Corps will explore the
                                balance between press freedom, government
                                transparency, and national security, while the
                                Nepal-focused House of Representatives will
                                bring valuable local relevance to the conference
                                by debating issues ranging from government
                                accountability and budget allocations to foreign
                                policy and beyond. Alongside these contemporary
                                discussions, delegates will also participate in
                                historical and imaginative simulations,
                                challenging them to think creatively, adapt to
                                complex scenarios, and engage with perspectives
                                beyond their own.
                            </p>
                            <p
                                style="color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.9; font-size: 1.05rem; font-style: italic; margin-top: 1.5rem;"
                            >
                                Since its inception in 2005, RBSMUN has earned a
                                reputation for excellence through the quality
                                and diversity of its committees and debates. I
                                am confident that this year's organising team
                                will continue that proud tradition led by
                                <strong
                                    >Pragyam Gautam as Secretary General, Ruhaan
                                    Bhatta and Raavya Shrestha as
                                    Deputy-Secretary Generals, and Prasiddha
                                    Mainali as Crisis Director.</strong
                                >
                            </p>
                            <p
                                style="color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.9; font-size: 1.05rem; font-style: italic; margin-top: 1.5rem;"
                            >
                                To all delegates—from Rato Bangala School and
                                schools across Nepal and beyond—I extend a warm
                                welcome. I encourage you to participate with
                                curiosity, integrity, and respect, to listen as
                                carefully as you speak, and to approach every
                                challenge with an open mind.
                            </p>
                            <p
                                style="color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.9; font-size: 1.05rem; font-style: italic; margin-top: 1.5rem;"
                            >
                                I wish you a rewarding, inspiring, and
                                successful RBSMUN 2026"
                            </p>
                            <p
                                style="color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.9; font-size: 1.05rem; font-style: italic; margin-top: 1.5rem;"
                            >
                                <strong>
                                    Milan Dixit<br />
                                    Principal, Rato Bangala School</strong
                                >
                            </p>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>
    </div>

    <footer class="footer">
        <div class="container">
            <div class="footer-grid">
                <div class="footer-col">
                    <h4 class="footer-logo">
                        RBS<span class="logo-accent">MUN</span>
                    </h4>
                </div>
                <div class="footer-col">
                    <h4>Navigate</h4>
                    <a href="/">Home</a>
                    <a href="/about">About Us</a>
                    <a href="/committees">Committees</a>
                    <a href="/conference">Conference Details</a>
                </div>
                <div class="footer-col">
                    <h4>Contact</h4>
                    <a href="mailto:contact@ratobangala.edu.np"
                        >contact@ratobangala.edu.np</a
                    >
                    <a href="tel:015447618">01-5447618</a>
                    <a href="tel:015447620">01-5447620</a>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="footer-bottom">
                <p>&copy; 2026 RBSMUN. All rights reserved.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </footer>
</Layout>
